    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive deployment against favorable matchups. The strongest play on the board is **Brice Turang** (73.40), who benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Lowder; his 19% SP Skill boost highlights the optimizer's confidence in his ability to capitalize on a weaker arm while batting in a prime three-hole position. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (67.04) and **Corbin Carroll** (66.84) are elite options today. **Corbin Carroll** remains a critical anchor for our scarce stolen base production, and despite a slight platoon penalty, his xwOBA profile and favorable spot in the order justify his near-elite status. **James Wood** (62.42) also warrants attention; despite facing a tougher matchup against Nola, his elite 0.404 xwOBA and top-of-the-order usage keep him well above the 60-point threshold for strong starts.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Travis Bazzana** (47.92), who narrowly missed the cut. While his leadoff positioning provides a 10% boost to his profile, the negative impact of a same-handed platoon against Murphy ultimately capped his efficiency, keeping him just shy of the active rotation. Conversely, **Austin Riley** (59.71) nearly reached the elite tier; his 12% SP Skill boost against Sears suggests a high ceiling for power production today. We are monitoring **Jose Caballero** (51.82) closely, as his match against Skubal presents significant risk; he remains in the lineup primarily due to his utility in stolen base accumulation, but we must acknowledge that Skubal\u2019s elite arm significantly lowers the floor for our middle infield output.\n\nWe are operating with a cautious eye toward the weather and the high-leverage arms scheduled for tonight. While **Gabriel Moreno** (55.24) and **Josh Naylor** (53.63) are solid plays, they are tethered to respectable pitchers in Liberatore and Ashcraft, respectively; both offer dependable production but lack the explosive matchup upside of **Brice Turang**. As we track these games, maintain focus on the SB-suppression tactics of opposing catchers, which has dampened the projected scores for players like **Max Muncy** and **Kyle Karros**. Should any late lineup changes occur, the bench depth of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** will remain sidelined as they currently fail to meet our aggressive 40.0 efficiency floor.",
